    "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2019 the syndicate's gross claims outstanding were 3,989.3 million (USD). During 2019 the syndicate recorded significant reserve movements driven primarily by natural catastrophe events (notably 2019 typhoons Hagibis and Faxai) and adverse development on prior-year catastrophe reserves (Typhoon Jebi), partly offset by reserve releases on prior large catastrophe events (Typhoon Mangkhut and Hurricanes Harvey, Irma and Maria). The syndicate also cites adverse impacts on its liability portfolio from US social inflation. On balance the gross claims development for prior underwriting years (2017 and earlier) was an adverse movement (strengthening) when measured on the gross claims development triangle.",
